<title>USA: U.S. corn growers see good acreage in South.</title>
<headline>U.S. corn growers see good acreage in South.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPA 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The president of the National Corn Growers Association (NCGA) Thursday said with cotton prices under pressure, corn growers expect there will be &quot;fairly good&quot; corn acreage in the Southern areas.</p>
<p>NCGA's Wallie Hardie also told a news conference to kick off a meeting of top corn and soybean growers that high soybean prices would be beneficial for all farmers this year, &quot;giving us an opportunity this summer to price our product at a profit.&quot;</p>
<p>Wallie predicted 1997/98 corn acreage at 81 million acres, matching the U.S. Agriculture Department's projection.</p>
</text>
